      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Spatial frame with an entire top-floor Y beam line missing\n\nReconstruct geometry and connectivity from the architectural input.dxf, interpreting its S-* structural lines and labels while filtering the A-* wall, column-footprint and equipment distractors. Reconcile the labelled orthographic views using properties.json dxfMapping. Read supports from properties.json boundaryConditions and the CAD annotations; use the matching member labels in assignments.json and loads.json. Section-detail images describe section properties and roll only. Member local direction follows DXF LINE start-to-end as specified in properties.json; no structural geometry image is supplied. Perform first-order linear elastic analysis using YJK; save the self-weight OFF and no-rigid-diaphragm settings. Use explicit section/material stiffness and signed right-handed global axes, Z upward. Retain actual load positions and distributed loads.\n\nReport all of the following for each stated selection, with signs and units:\n- Global Ux of the loaded top corner n2-2-2 [case-D-D-loaded-corner-ux]\n- Global Uy of the loaded top corner n2-2-2 [case-D-D-loaded-corner-uy]\n- Global Uy of the top-floor center node n1-1-2 [case-D-D-top-center-uy]\n\nProvide labelled model and result figures consistent with the numerical values. Preserve the input-to-model ID mapping, engine version/settings, current execution log, original result tables and figure data. If an essential datum is missing, ask specifically for it before analysis.\n",
